many schools across venezuela have  reopened their classrooms 19 months  after the pandemic forced them to close  and after several delays due to rising  rates of infection  we've created the conditions to return  safely to classrooms the administrations  and the teachers have been working to  make sure the return is safe so that  parents feel comfortable  after so long without face-to-face  learning or playing with his friends  juan is clear about what he expects from  school  he says he wants two things to play and  to learn  his mother miriam says she was nervous  about the return but it was necessary  is happy to be coming back they needed  communication with other kids to play to  share things with their teachers that  motivation  the government has called the reopening  campaign a drop of love for my school  this video released on one of president  nicolas maduro's social media accounts  shows workers sprucing up school  buildings and the state delivering vital  learning equipment although he admits  many pupils have abandoned their  education  [Music]  we'll invite them back so they can  return to the classroom  however many teachers and parents say  buildings are in disrepair supplies are  low and thousands of teachers the lowest  paid in the region have left the  profession or join the millions who have  fled venezuela to escape poverty and  inflation  i don't think the conditions are  suitable for children to return there  are schools that lack water that are not  equipped that don't have the  infrastructure  many teachers like johanna have  supplemented their meager incomes by  inviting pupils into their homes  we are very concerned because we are  going to find many gaps in their  education for example if they were in  first grade when the pandemic began  they have already passed the second or  third and maybe they don't know how to  read  official figures say the virus has  killed less than 5 000 people in  venezuela and infected four hundred  thousand however many health experts  dispute those numbers as well as the  government claim that it has vaccinated  eighty percent of teachers  the welcome return to school in  venezuela is proving to be fraught with  difficulties with the kovit 19 pandemic  highlighting and exacerbating many of  the problems the country's education  system was already facing  [Music]  al jazeera
 

